content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-112 — AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-22300",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Flow: the reported approximately 20% reduction over two weeks at unchanged valve settings matches the manual's 'Low flow or head' symptom, so its troubleshooting actions apply. The HF-300 rating is 300 m3/h at 45 m head, but this is a rated operating point, not a documented percentage-drop alarm limit. Absolute before/after flow and head are not reported, so operation relative to the rating cannot be determined.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vibration: Figure 3's HF-300 limits apply to vibration velocity in mm/s RMS measured on the bearing housings. If the reported 2.0 mm/s was measured on that basis, it falls in Zone A (0.0–2.8 mm/s RMS, 'New machines'), 0.8 mm/s below the Zone A/B boundary at 2.8. It is below Zone C (4.5–7.1, restricted/plan maintenance) and Zone D (7.1–11.0, damage likely/stop the pump). Both bearing housings must be checked weekly and the highest reading classified; the report does not confirm that this was done.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Temperature: the HF-300 bearing-housing surface limits apply to the reported 65 C housing reading. It is within the normal range (normal up to 70 C), 15 C below the 80 C alarm and 25 C below the 90 C trip. It is not above the manufacturer's alarm limit, so the site rule requiring a priority-1 work order within the shift is not triggered by this reading.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Leakage: no leakage is reported, so the troubleshooting symptom 'Leakage at shaft seal' does not presently support seal replacement on that basis. This does not by itself establish the internal condition of the seal, impeller or wear rings.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Immediate-stop assessment: the reported vibration, if confirmed as a bearing-housing RMS reading, is not in the manufacturer's highest severity zone, and the housing temperature is below the trip value. Current evidence therefore does not require an immediate stop; any later Zone D classification would require immediate stopping and reliability-engineer notification before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "1. Worn impeller: investigate this first because it is a documented cause of low flow or head and is consistent with a gradual performance decline. Inspect the impeller and wear rings; the current readings do not confirm the diagnosis.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "2. Air in the suction: this is another documented cause of low flow or head. Check for air and vent the casing as directed by the troubleshooting table.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "3. Closed valve: a closed valve is also documented as a cause. Unchanged settings make a newly closed valve less consistent with the history, but do not prove actual valve position, so verify it rather than excluding this cause without a check.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "1. Before internal work, record the actual flow and head and establish the pre-degradation baseline for comparison with the 300 m3/h at 45 m rating. Confirm that the 2.0 mm/s vibration value is RMS, measure both bearing housings, classify the highest value with Figure 3, and repeat the housing-surface temperature measurement.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "2. Check the actual valve position for a closed-valve condition, check for air in the suction, and vent the casing. Continue weekly vibration monitoring on both bearing housings while the pump remains in service.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "3. If these checks do not resolve the low-flow condition, internally inspect the pump under the isolation and line-break controls. Use the back pull-out design to remove the rotating assembly without disturbing the casing or pipework; the 68 kg assembly requires the specified lifting controls.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "4. Inspect the impeller and wear rings and record their condition. If the impeller must be removed, follow the back pull-out/impeller removal sequence. Do not condemn components against an assumed wear limit: none is supplied in the evidence. On refitting, tighten the M24 impeller nut to 160 Nm under Table 5's lightly-oiled-thread condition.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "5. Only if inspection establishes a need for mechanical-seal replacement, follow procedure 5.2: withdraw the seal and sleeve, inspect the sleeve for scoring, and fit the new seal with a new casing gasket. For this serial, do not fit HF3-450; use pre-set cartridge seal HF3-450B. No sleeve measurement is needed to set the pre-set cartridge, but replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 separately if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "6. Inspect bearings only as warranted by the opened scope and their condition. Replace both bearings as a pair if either shows wear, noise or high temperature; the reported 65 C housing reading alone is normal and is not grounds for bearing replacement.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "7. On reassembly, for lightly oiled threads and only where disturbed, tighten casing bolts M16 to 210 Nm, impeller nut M24 to 160 Nm, and bearing-housing bolts M12 to 85 Nm. If HF3-450B is fitted, tighten its seal gland nuts to 30 Nm under SB-2026-014, not the superseded 25 Nm manual value for this asset.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "8. Use a laser alignment tool after any work that moves the motor or bearing housing. Meet the documented tolerances: parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular 0.05 mm per 100 mm. Alignment is not automatically required for work that moves neither component.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "9. Before return to service, confirm the permitted isolation/plant handover steps are complete and maintain Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge; never run the seal dry. After restart, check for leakage and record flow/head, both-housing vibration and housing temperature against the same documented criteria.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C09",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Conditional part only: one pre-set cartridge mechanical seal if inspection authorises seal replacement. Mandatory substitute for HF3-450 on serial HF3-22300; do not fit HF3-450 on this pump.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Conditional part only: one shaft sleeve if removed for seal work and scoring is found to exceed 0.1 mm depth.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "Not specified in evidence",
      "description": "Conditional part only: one new casing gasket required when mechanical-seal replacement is performed; confirm the correct part number before ordering.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "For any work inside the pump or on its seal, apply electrical isolation and lock-out/tag-out at the MCC, mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves, and obtain a line-break permit after draining and venting first.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg, exceeding the site's 25 kg lifting threshold. Before lifting it, obtain a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and use certified lifting equipment; the manufacturer also requires lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the line is chemically dosed, wear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves. Chemical dosing is not stated in the fault report and must be confirmed before work.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Maintain Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the seal dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If subsequent monitoring classifies vibration in Zone D, stop the pump immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart. Zone D is documented as 'Damage likely - stop the pump'.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If bearing-housing temperature rises above the 80 C manufacturer alarm limit, raise a priority-1 work order within the shift; the manufacturer's trip value is 90 C.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Initial low-flow troubleshooting and impeller/wear-ring inspection: Table 6 provides no standard labour time for this diagnostic scope; do not represent the conditional replacement times below as the confirmed initial duration.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If mechanical-seal replacement is authorised: 4.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If bearing condition requires replacement of the pair: 6.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If motor or bearing-housing movement requires laser alignment: 1.5 hours with 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal gland torque conflict: manual Table 5 lists M10 seal gland nuts at 25 Nm, whereas SB-2026-014 specifies 30 Nm for HF3-450B. The bulletin, issued 14 March 2026, applies to HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above; P-112 is HF3-22300, so the bulletin governs this asset. Use 30 Nm for any HF3-450B installation; the below-serial instruction to retain HF3-450 and Table 5 does not apply.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal applicability decision: for this in-range serial, SB-2026-014 prohibits fitting HF3-450 and requires HF3-450B instead. The manual's generic replacement sequence and new-casing-gasket requirement still apply, while the bulletin controls the seal part, its pre-set installation and the gland torque.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "What are the measured current and pre-degradation flow and head, and what production impact or required restoration date follows from the approximately 20% loss? The evidence does not define site criteria for choosing between P2 and P3.",
    "Was the 2.0 mm/s vibration reading RMS and taken on a bearing housing, which housing was measured, and what was the highest reading across both housings? Which housing gave the 65 C surface-temperature reading?",
    "Did inspection find impeller/wear-ring wear, air in the suction or an actually closed valve? No root cause is confirmed by the report.",
    "What are the impeller and wear-ring acceptance/wear limits and their replacement part numbers? They are not supplied in the evidence.",
    "Is internal disassembly required, and has any seal or bearing defect actually been found? The conditional seal, sleeve, bearing and alignment work should not be converted into confirmed scope without findings.",
    "If seal replacement becomes necessary, what is the casing-gasket part number? If bearing replacement becomes necessary, what are the bearing part numbers?",
    "Is this a chemically dosed line, requiring chemical goggles and nitrile gloves?",
    "What labour duration should be assigned to the initial diagnostics and any impeller/wear-ring repair? Table 6 only covers seal replacement, bearing-pair replacement and laser alignment."
  ]
}
